gbench fix for the SWE-ReX (swe-rex 1.4.0) that SWE-agent-for-eval vendors, applied by
gbench/docker/sweagent_for_eval.Dockerfile to the copy in the image's venv
(venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/swerex). Paths are relative to that site-packages directory.

swerex/runtime/local.py (the bash session the runtime server in every task container runs):
BashSession split every command with bashlex 0.18 and joined the pieces with " ; ". A heredoc
whose operator is not the last word of its line (`cat <<EOF > f`, `python3 - <<EOF 2>&1`,
`cat <<EOF | sh`) lost its body and terminator, and a heredoc followed by another command got that
command on its terminator's line, so the shell waited for a terminator that never came until the
command timed out (SWE-agent-for-eval: 90 minutes). A command holding a heredoc operator is now
never split: its exact text goes to a file and the session runs `eval "$(cat FILE; rm -f FILE)"`,
which bash parses as it parses a script (one line sent, one prompt, the file gone before the first
command runs). Also: a piece that ends with the background operator `&` is no longer followed by
" ; " (`a &` then `b` became the syntax error `a & ; b`). Every other command is split and joined
as before.

swerex/deployment/docker.py: glibc_dockerfile, which builds the runtime layer of every task
container, installed the latest swe-rex from PyPI. It now installs swe-rex 1.4.0 and its
dependencies at pinned versions (no resolution) and writes this patched local.py over swe-rex
1.4.0's own, checking both files by sha256.

